// gc-design.md §5.4 (Stage 28 W15a1): a no-GC region that alone
// allocates more than AVANT_HEAP_MAX_MB. avant_str_split keeps its parts in
// one defer region (C35's fix), and no collection may run inside it
// (C32), so its allocation proceeds past the limit and the full collection
// runs after the region; when the region by itself is over the limit, no
// collection after it could bring the heap back under it, and the program
// dies with "heap limit in a no-GC region (<helper>)". The live set
// outside the split is small: 300,000 one-letter words (600 KB of text)
// split into 300,000 strings and their array, about 10 MB in the region.
// Under AVANT_HEAP_MAX_MB=4 it dies so; without a limit it prints the
// part count.

fn main {
  b = buf_new()
  i = 0
  while i < 300000 {
    b.push_str("x ")
    i = i + 1
  }
  text = b.to_s
  parts = text.split(" ")
  puts("parts: ${parts.size}")
}
